Errno: harvest the E* names from a stub TU the engine cc expands.

Errno.pm's generator scans the target's errno.h AS A FILE (via
$sysroot/usr/include + locincpth) for the E* macro names, then reads their
values by preprocessing `#include <errno.h>`. Under the engine the musl
headers are virtual (inside clang), so the file scan finds nothing ("No error
definitions found"). The value step already works, so only the name harvest
changes: get_files returns a stub TU that `clang -E -dM` expands to every E*.
Linux crosses only; the native build finds errno.h via engineIncFix's
locincpth.

--- a/ext/Errno/Errno_pm.PL
+++ b/ext/Errno/Errno_pm.PL
@@ -106,7 +106,7 @@
     return "$cppstdin $Config{cppflags} $Config{cppminus}";
 }
 
-sub get_files {
+sub get_files { if (open(my $s, ">", "unpin_errno.c")) { print $s "#include <errno.h>\n"; close $s; return ("unpin_errno.c"); }
     my @file;
     # When cross-compiling we may store a path for gcc's "sysroot" option:
     my $sysroot = $Config{sysroot} || '';
